<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
   Backup and device-transfer rules for API 31+ (`android:dataExtractionRules`).

   Backup is currently disabled outright — see `android:allowBackup="false"` and the reasoning above
   it in AndroidManifest.xml. These rules are therefore not consulted today. They exist so that the
   exclusion survives anyone turning backup back on.

   Both destinations are listed on purpose. `<cloud-backup>` is the one that uploads; `<device-transfer>`
   never leaves the user's hands, but a captured log is a third party's data rather than the user's,
   so it should not silently follow them onto a new phone either. Neither is a decision Loki should
   make on the user's behalf, so both are excluded and the user re-captures if they want the data.

   `logs/` is `SavedLogs.logsDir`, relative to `filesDir`. The two spellings have to agree. Cache is
   never included by the platform, so the temp capture and `log_shares/` need no line here — see
   backup_rules.xml.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude
            domain="file"
            path="logs/" />
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <exclude
            domain="file"
            path="logs/" />
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
